      "asciiScore": 0.0,
      "whoisText": "Durmegil Guldur, Collector of Lost\n    Souls is a Maia (Cartographer).\nLast login 5 months and 4 days ago from\n    [numerical address].\nOriginally a Maia in the service of Námo, Durmegil joined Melkor in Utumno, for\nthe Dark Lord had promised to allow him to venture forth and collect the souls\nof the dead for him. When Utumno was sacked and destroyed by the Valar, rather\nthan face their judgement, Durmegil fled formless into the far reaches of the\nArda, drawn to the places of the dead.  As such, he spent the most of the First\nand Second Ages of the World drifting through the deep, dark places of Arda.\n\nAt the rise of Sauron, his presence was sensed by Olórin as he infiltrated the\ndungeons of Dol Guldur, where Durmegil had been drawn by the presence of the\nNazgûl. Though his spirit had been darkened by years of walking the paths of\nthe dead, Olórin sensed that Durmegil was not evil, and so counselled him to\ntravel into the West and seek the pardon of the Valar.  Námo agreed that he\ncould resume his service if he would travel to Middle-Earth as an emissary,\nhelping the Free Peoples, and destroying the minions of Sauron.\n",
